I've finally gotten around to publishing a local patch I've been using
for a few years.

I like the principle of the "menucolors" patch, but it has an annoying
flaw.  It is natural to want to highlight known-uncursed items
differently than unknown-buc-status items, but nethack makes this
difficult by eliding the word "uncursed" whenever the player could infer
it.

As a result, no such menucolors ruleset can be correct for both priests
and non-priests, and the version for non-priests must effectively
incorporate a complete list of nethack's armor items.

So, I've modified the interface between nethack and its window modules
to provide hints, and created my own "enhanced menucolors" patch that
takes advantage of it.  Using special codes designed not to collide with
valid regexps, you can specify a rule to match only based on the hints.

A simple example emenucolors config is:

 MENUCOLOR="B^"=blue
 MENUCOLOR="U^"=green
 MENUCOLOR="C^"=red
 MENUCOLOR="C^(being worn)"=orange
 MENUCOLOR="O^ wand of cancellation"=yellow
 MENUCOLOR="O^ wand called cancellation"=yellow

So much simpler than the minimal correct menucolors-1.5 config that
would do the same thing.

The patch is in two parts, to be applied in order.  The first modifies
the API and corrects all window-system modules to (hopefully) not break.
The second is the modified version of menucolors that uses the new
information.

ftp://talamasca.ocis.net/pub/michael/beta/nethack-3.4.3-emcapi-1.diff
ftp://talamasca.ocis.net/pub/michael/beta/nethack-3.4.3-emenucolors-1.diff

Note that while all window systems are patched by emcapi, emenucolors
only provides colorization on the same platforms as menucolors-1.5.

